
v2 updates 1 aug 2025 20:54 

Added
FastAPI framework Switched from Flask to FastAPI, leveraging its built-in async support, automatic OpenAPI docs, and data validation.

Configuration via environment variables

PYTT_ENV controls development vs. production mode.

DATABASE_URL (defaulting to a SQLite file) drives SQLAlchemy connection strings.

Structured logging Configured Python’s logging for DEBUG in development and INFO in production, integrating with Uvicorn’s logger.

SQLAlchemy integration

Created engine, SessionLocal and get_db dependency for per-request DB sessions.

Enables clean transaction management and easy dependency injection.

CORS middleware Added CORSMiddleware to allow cross-origin requests (locked down later for production).

Health check & root endpoints

GET /health returns status ok.

GET / returns a welcome message with the app title and version.

Global exception handlers

404 handler returns JSON { "detail": "Resource not found" }.

500 handler logs the error and returns JSON { "detail": "Internal server error" }.

Router registration

Included users, events, timeslots, and calendar routers under /users, /events, /timeslots, /calendar.

Applied tags for automatic grouping in the generated OpenAPI docs.

Injected the get_db dependency at the router level for consistent session access.

Uvicorn startup entrypoint Configured uvicorn.run with hot-reload in development, dynamic port binding via PORT, and log-level toggled by environment.

Changed
Reorganized project structure to align with FastAPI best practices (separating configuration, DB setup, routers, and middleware).

Notes
Future improvements: tighten CORS origins, add request-validation schemas (Pydantic), and integrate calendar APIs or ICS export functionality.
